!!! archon/engine/patterns.mat
!!! Text primitives shared by the scanning engine.
!!!
!!! `split-lines` is implemented here in Matrix rather than delegating to
!!! `ny.lang.text::split_lines`, because that Ny function returns a
!!! `ny::lang::collections::vec<text>`, which a Matrix page cannot consume as an
!!! `array of text`. The tier-one helpers `char_at` and `substring` are enough.

book archon.engine.patterns

read everything from ny.lang.core
read everything from ny.lang.text

!!! Split a text buffer into lines. The result always holds at least one
!!! element; a trailing newline yields a final empty element.
public split-lines receives content as text returns array of text begin paragraph
    variable lines as array of text is []
    value total as number is the length of content
    variable start as number is 0
    variable cursor as number is 0
    repeat while cursor is less than total
        value ch is ny.lang.text::char_at with s being content, index being cursor
        when ch equals newline then
            append (ny.lang.text::substring with s being content, start being start, length being (cursor minus start)) to lines
            set start to cursor plus 1
        end when
        set cursor to cursor plus 1
    end repeat
    append (ny.lang.text::substring with s being content, start being start, length being (total minus start)) to lines
    give lines
end paragraph

!!! True when the line contains the needle as a literal substring.
public line-contains receives line as text, needle as text returns boolean begin paragraph
    give ny.lang.text::contains with s being line, needle being needle
end paragraph

!!! How many times the needle occurs in the line.
public needle-count receives line as text, needle as text returns number begin paragraph
    give ny.lang.text::count with s being line, needle being needle
end paragraph
